<Addin>
  <!--
    Tells VS4Mac's MEF container to scan this addin's own assembly for
    [Export] components: specifically MdixLanguageClient (implements
    ILanguageClient) and MdixContentDefinition's exports, both in
    MdixLanguageClient.cs. Without this, the host's Mono.Addins loader picks
    the assembly up fine, but MEF composition (a separate mechanism layered
    on top, not something Mono.Addins does for you automatically) never
    finds those exports, so ILanguageClient never activates for .mdix files
    even though the addin itself loads without error.

    File name matches AssemblyName in MdixAddin.csproj, namely "MdixLanguageSupport" —
    not the class name "MdixLanguageClient" or the project name "MdixAddin".

    Source: Matt Ward's own VS4Mac LSP walkthrough (lastexitcode.com,
    "Language Server Protocol support in Visual Studio for Mac 7.4"),
    "Enabling Managed Extensibility Framework Support" section.
  -->
  <Extension path="/MonoDevelop/Ide/Composition">
    <Assembly file="MdixLanguageSupport.dll" />
  </Extension>

  <Extension path="/MonoDevelop/Core/MimeTypes">
    <MimeType
        id="text/x-mdix"
        _description="DixScript Configuration File"
        icon="md-mdix-file"
        isText="true">
      <File pattern="*.mdix" />
    </MimeType>
  </Extension>

  <!--
    2026-08-03 — ROOT CAUSE OF THE INSTALL WARNING ("is trying to extend
    '/MonoDevelop/Ide/StockIcons', but there isn't any add-in defining this
    extension point") and, most likely, the folder-expand/dropdown issue:
    wrong top-level namespace. Confirmed against mono/monodevelop's actual
    current source (github.com/mono/monodevelop) — every real addin that
    registers a StockIcon (MonoDevelop.Deployment, MonoDevelop.XmlEditor,
    MonoDevelop.DotNetCore, MonoDevelop.Refactoring, MonoDevelop.Profiling,
    Unity-Technologies/MonoDevelop.UnityMode) extends
    "/MonoDevelop/Core/StockIcons" — under Core, not Ide. That extension
    point genuinely doesn't exist under Ide, which is exactly what the
    install warning said and why the icon registration was silently
    dropped. Since the MimeType extension above references icon=
    "md-mdix-file", and that stock icon was therefore never actually
    registered, resolving it while rendering a .mdix file's tree node is
    the most likely cause of the folder not expanding.

    resource="mdix-file.svg" also corrected earlier to match the file that
    actually exists in Resources/ (mdix-file-icon.svg never did).
  -->
  <Extension path="/MonoDevelop/Core/StockIcons">
    <StockIcon stockid="md-mdix-file" resource="mdix-file.svg" />
  </Extension>

  <Extension path="/MonoDevelop/Ide/FileFilters">
    <FileFilter id="Mdix" _label="DixScript Files" extensions="*.mdix" />
  </Extension>
</Addin>
